Description: CVE-2025-15661 - Avoid out-of-bounds read in sftp_symlink on malformed packet
 A malicious SSH server or MITM can send a crafted SSH_FXP_NAME response with
 link_len exceeding the actual packet data during SFTP READLINK/REALPATH,
 causing a heap over-read up to target_len-1 bytes due to missing packet
 buffer size validation before memcpy in sftp_symlink() in src/sftp.c.
 .
 Backported from upstream commit 2dae3024 (PR #1717) to libssh2 1.9.0.
 The upstream patch uses a string_buf to bounds-check every read from the
 response packet. Adaptations for 1.9.0:
   * _libssh2_get_byte() does not exist in 1.9.0 - replaced with
     _libssh2_check_length(&buf, 1) followed by a direct byte read and
     pointer advance (semantically equivalent).
   * LIBSSH2_UNCONST is not in 1.9.0 - dropped because `data` is already
     unsigned char * (non-const), so a direct assignment suffices.
 .
