+# CVE-2026-66035 — Not Affected on Debian Bullseye libssh2 1.9.0
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| **CVE** | CVE-2026-66035 |
+| **Component** | libssh2 ETM decrypt path (`src/transport.c`) |
+| **Package** | libssh2 1.9.0-2+deb11u1 |
+| **Assessment** | **Not affected** — vulnerable code not present |
+| **VEX justification** | `vulnerable_code_not_present` |
+| **CWE** | CWE-122 (Heap Buffer Overflow) |
+| **Upstream fix** | commit `42e33d81577ed4b95d4b4f6f845e5ee8efe5eeb4` (PR #2198) |
+
+---
+
+## Summary
+
+CVE-2026-66035 requires the Encrypt-then-MAC transport decrypt path that
+allocates `decrypt_size` and copies `blocksize - 1` bytes. That feature
+landed in libssh2 **1.11.0**. Bullseye's 1.9.0 has no `.etm` /
+`decrypt_buffer` logic; the only similar first-block copy is already
+guarded by `if(blocksize - 5 <= (int) total_num)`.
+
+## Verification
+
+```bash
+grep -nE '\.etm|decrypt_size|decrypt_buffer' src/transport.c
+# Expected: no matches
+```
+
+## Version comparison
+
+| Release | libssh2 | Status |
+|---------|---------|--------|
+| bullseye | 1.9.0-2+deb11u1 | **not-affected** |
+| bookworm | 1.10.0-3 | **not-affected** |
+| 1.11.x until 42e33d8 | vulnerable | needs upstream fix |
+
+## References
+
+- https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-66035
+- https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/42e33d81577ed4b95d4b4f6f845e5ee8efe5eeb4
+- https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/pull/987 (ETM introduction)
+
+**CVE-2026-66035 is not-affected on libssh2 1.9.0-2+deb11u1.**
